= Information — Technical =

== Probabilistic information ==
For event x with probability p(x):

<pre>
I(x) = -log_b p(x)
</pre>

The logarithm base determines units such as bits or nats.

== Semantic boundary ==
Shannon information depends on probability distributions over symbols/events.

Semantic content requires additional representational, interpretive, or truth conditions not contained in the Shannon measure itself.

== Physical and computational uses ==
Information can be embodied in physical states, encoded in symbols, or represented computationally.

Claims that information is “physical” concern implementation and physical constraints, not an identity between all informational and semantic concepts.

